    "updated_at": "2026-11-11T22:11:35Z",
    "body": "Maintainer direction (2026-11-11): \"cps files should be tested against the post binary with a couple of edge case intermediary files to parse.\"\n\nSo the shape of this issue is decided, and it is wider than the ten tests in the body: every shipped post script (`assets/posts/*.cps`) gets a suite in `crates/post/tests` that runs the post engine itself on a small set of recorded intermediate toolpath files (`.cl`) and compares the program text - no `camcraft_app`, no toolpath generation in the test.\n\n- The intermediate files are a handful of deliberate edge cases shared by all posts, not one per existing test: e.g. arcs in each plane and a helix, a full circle, a canned drilling cycle with a retract change, a tool change with a spindle direction change, a rotary index and a tilted move (so posts that cannot do it show their named refusal), a probing cycle, an empty section, very small and very large coordinates.\n- Each post's expected output (or its named refusal) for each file is a golden beside the suite.\n- The existing app-side post suites keep covering the document-to-post path; where one only repeats what the new suite pins, it can go.\n\n#923 then has an exact target: a change to `assets/posts/<name>.cps` selects that post's suite in `crates/post/tests`.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
