    "body": "test on issue/926-post-script-suites · PR #1002 · pinned by script_carvera, script_doosan_dnm, script_fanuc, script_fanuc_lathe, script_haas, script_heidenhain, script_mazak, script_sinumerik, script_tormach, script_tormach_lathe, script_tormach_plasma, recorded_streams (post) and recorded_post_streams (app) · merges when reviewed\n\nSlice 1 landed there (`Refs #926`, not `Fixes`): nine recorded `.cnc` edge-case streams in `crates/post/tests/recorded/streams/`, one suite per shipped `.cps` running the post binary on them against goldens or named refusals, and generator-side staleness guards (post for the cl-built streams, app for the motion-built probe and drill streams, round-trip for the one hand-written stream).\n\nLeft for slice 2 (what keeps this issue open):\n- Move the ten app tests in the body (`fanuc_post`, `probe_dialects`, `probe_guard`, `probe_report`, `probe_tormach`, `inverted_probe`, `arc_planes`, `inverted_equivalence`, `inverted_post`, `vertical_arc_entry`) to `crates/post/tests`, reading recorded input. Several are touched by the open PRs #967 / #972, so this should follow their merges. Where a moved test only repeats what a script suite now pins, it can go (maintainer's note).\n- Once #996 lands, the runner can pass `tilthead.mch` straight to the binary instead of the mirrored file.\n\nPost bugs the suites found, filed and listed as known bugs (no golden) in `crates/post/tests/recorded/mod.rs`: #994 (P0, canned-cycle hop at the R plane), #995 (P1, flood coolant in a probe section), #996 (P1, CLI ignores a vendor .mch), #997 (P2, fanuc C0 word), #998 (P2, plasma refusal wording).\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
